{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the width.</b> Now the width is half the length. The commentators said that the Tabernacle was placed at a distance of fifty on the west, and its width was fifty, and this is <b>and the width fifty by fifty</b>. In my opinion, the reason is that it is because of the length of its corners being upright, for its width on every side is fifty. And there is no reason for the meaning of 'fifty by fifty' to be from the side of the court, for it did not repeat the length over the width as expected."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:43.048716237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}